# Boron 2P with its p electron in the complex m=+1 orbital, in a
# magnetic field B=-0.05 along z. Within a symmetry block the Zeeman term
# is a constant, so E(+B)-E(-B) = -B (M_L + 2 M_S) = -0.1 exactly
# (M_L=1, M_S=1/2); the complex_orbs_b_ml_p and _m references satisfy it.
System B.xyz
Basis cc-pVDZ
Method lda_x-lda_c_vwn
Multiplicity 2
Restricted false
ComplexBasis true
LinearOccupations -1
LinearOccupationFile complex_orbs_b_ml.linocc
LinearB -0.05
JKMethod Cholesky
DFTGrid 75 -302
# The orbital gradient has a noise floor of a few 1e-9, which some runs
# do not get below; the energy is checked to 1e-7
ConvThr 1e-8
SaveChk complex_orbs_b_ml_m.chk
